KG42.register("rules-8df768b56a292714ea42448c",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R007","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The local energy product is electricity; there are no heat sales to customers at node D in this coalition. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor}. Local MG energy supply includes electricity and cogenerated heat. Residential customers may purchase heat from the MG investor or supply their own heat. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {Private investor, D}. The local energy products purchased by MG customers comprise electricity and heat from MG CHP operation. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {Private investor, D}. | Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}. | Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor}.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e026"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product is electricity; there are no heat sales to customers at node D in this coalition. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor}.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e026"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local MG energy supply includes electricity and cogenerated heat. Residential customers may purchase heat from the MG investor or supply their own heat. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {Private investor, D}.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e019"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy products purchased by MG customers comprise electricity and heat from MG CHP operation. Scope: Local MG supply to customers at node D in Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D}.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-e020"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ity’s proﬁt and the surplus of customers at distribution node D when they are served by the utility.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The value of Coalition {VIU, Private investor} is the sum of profit for the utility and the private investor, if the MG only provides power to residential customers. The utility could cooperate with the private investor to satisfy the electric load of customers at node D because distributed generation is less subject to siting limitations than new centralized power plants. In this case, the utility relies on the MG for local provision of energy, and remunerates electricity sales and ancillary services to the grid. However, since consumers at node D are not part of the coalition, they continue to supply their thermal load with natural gas furnaces and Combined Heat and Power (CHP) capacity is not needed in the MG. The utility provides power to the other nodes, whose customers also satisfy their thermal load autonomously."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The utility provides power to the other nodes, whose customers also satisfy their thermal load auton","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Instead of relying on the VIU, customers at node D could cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration. MG generators would also supply reactive power needed by those consumers on a local basis. The value of Coalition {Private investor, D} is the sum of the private investor’s profit and the surplus of customers representing the MG load component. We assume that the utility can effectively prevent the MG from selling excess power and ancillary services to the grid, while still being required to act as a back-up supplier for microgrid customers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The utility provides power to the other nodes, whose customers also satisfy their thermal load auton","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The seventh (or grand) coalition is formed when all players act in concert. In this case, the private investor cooperates with both the utility and local customers at node D, with distributed generators satisfying their electric and thermal load. The value of Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D} is the sum of surpluses for the three players."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"in Tables 4 and 5, with the exception of the capital cost of natural gas reciprocating engines, whic","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We assume that MG customers pay an electricity price such that the private gains (or losses) from the grand coalition are split equally between them and the private investor. This result could be achieved through a profit-sharing mechanism, similar to the ones in the Energy Performance Contracts between Energy Service Companies (ESCOs) and their customers. The MG can also import electricity, as needed, at the regulated price of power. Residential customers can supply their own heat, at a natural gas price of $12.22/MBtu, or purchase heat from the MG investor at a 20% discount. The MG is subject to the same charges described for Coalition {VIU, Private investor}, although in this case they do not represent a transfer between parties in the same coalition. Finally, similarly to Coalition {VIU, Private investor}, we assume that the MG has islanding capability and provides reliability benefits to its customers (equal to their avoided cost of a three-hour per year power interruption)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"r 2.3.6. Coalition {VIU, Private investor, D} The data used to simulate the grand coalition is the s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Like Coalition {Private investor, D}, MG customers pay an electricity price such that the private gains (or losses) from the grand coalition are split in equal parts between them and the private investor, and purchase heat from CHP operation of the MG at a 20% discount, relative to the cost of supplying their own heat."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e026","location":{"location_id":"src-43db3c92a3-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"C. Lo Prete, B.F. Hobbs / Applied En tive is to maximize surplus, given by the gross beneﬁt associat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Coalition {VIU, Private investor} also maximizes profits, subject to network and generator constraints. However, while the regulated utility’s profit is zero, the private investor is not subject to cost-of-service regulation and receives the regulated power price for its sales to local customers. Given the regulated price, the private investor can earn a profit or operate at a loss. In the latter case, the value of the coalition is set to zero: this is equivalent to assuming that no utility-sponsored MG is built, if unprofitable. As previously noted, a key difference with respect to the next two coalitions is that there are no heat sales to consumers at node D."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule defines which energy products are supplied or purchased under each coalition; the frozen graph and supplied quotations contain no design-selection or operational decision variable for the product definition.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric input, coefficient, price, efficiency, or domain parameter is part of this product-composition rule. Values in surrounding evidence, such as natural-gas prices or heat discounts, belong to pricing/trade passages and are not used in the local-energy-product definition here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","quote":"In this case, the utility relies on the MG for local provision of energy, and remunerates electricity sales and ancillary services to the grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e026","quote":"As previously noted, a key difference with respect to the next two coalitions is that there are no heat sales to consumers at node D."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","quote":"Instead of relying on the VIU, customers at node D could cooperate with the private investor to satisfy their electric and thermal load through cogeneration."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e019","quote":"Residential customers can supply their own heat, at a natural gas price of $12.22/MBtu, or purchase heat from the MG investor at a 20% discount."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","quote":"In this case, the private investor cooperates with both the utility and local customers at node D, with distributed generators satisfying their electric and thermal load."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e020","quote":"Like Coalition {Private investor, D}, MG customers pay an electricity price such that the private gains (or losses) from the grand coalition are split in equal parts between them and the private investor, and purchase heat from CHP operation of the MG at a 20% discount, relative to the cost of supplying their own heat."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5f8992de099e3b07587452bab114080a9f895fb88ede15fc9452024c094a39d7","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a qualitative, coalition-scoped definition of the local energy product: electricity alone in Coalition {VIU, Private investor}; electricity plus cogenerated heat when customers at D cooperate with the private investor; and electricity plus heat from MG CHP operation in the grand coalition. The supplied B quotations state product composition and scope, not an equation, optimization objective, variable domain, or numeric parameter belonging to this rule. B evidence remains unreviewed; this formalization therefore preserves the C.1 procedural statements without adding invented mathematics.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a unary product-scope restriction on product.local_energy for Coalition {VIU, Private investor}; the frozen graph has no edge representing product composition, so the constraint attaches only to the declared node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is a unary product-scope statement on product.local_energy for Coalition {Private investor, D}; no product-composition edge exists in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 is a unary product-scope statement on product.local_energy for the grand coalition; no product-composition edge exists in the frozen graph."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
